// KNOWN LIMITATION — should verify, currently rejected.
//
// The perm-sign side condition of `acc(x.f, p)` is discharged without the facts
// established by *earlier* parts of the same specification: `0/1 < p` is already
// stated, so `p` is provably positive by the time the `acc` is evaluated. Both the
// separate-clause and the `&&` form fail identically, so it is not about clause
// splitting — the side condition simply does not see the preceding conjunct.
//
// Silicon accepts both: `&&` is short-circuiting and `requires` clauses are
// evaluated in order, so `0 < p` is in the path condition before the `acc`.
//
// Found 2026-07-30 while trying to build a symbolic-fraction canary for the
// pc-alias consume path (invariant 7) — the inability to hold a symbolic
// non-negative fraction is why that path is only covered with concrete fractions.
// Tracked in design/block-vmir/PROGRESS.md.

field f: Int

method n(x: Ref, p: Perm)
    requires 0/1 < p
    requires acc(x.f, p)
{}
